messages:
maria: Found a gap in the migration guide: examples still check HTTP status codes. v2 will send structured errors (e.g. {code: 'RATE_LIMIT'}). We need an appendix mapping old codes to new codes and short tolerant snippets for customers.
kevin: Good catch. Let's add a tiny canonical table and recommendation to prefer error.code for alerts.
nina: I'll open a docs PR to add: 1) mapping table, 2) appendix describing retry semantics, 3) minimal py/ts snippets showing v2-first detection with v1 fallback, 4) update snippets folder and CI smoke tests. Targeting a draft by EOD Thu.
sam: Snippets to include (short):
```python
try:
    resp = client.generate(prompt)
except Exception as e:
    payload = getattr(e, 'meta', None) or getattr(e, 'body', None) or {}
    code = payload.get('code') or getattr(e, 'status_code', None)
    if code == 'RATE_LIMIT' or code == 429:
        backoff_and_retry()
    else:
        raise
```
```ts
try {
  await client.responses.create({ input: prompt });
} catch (err) {
  const code = err?.response?.data?.code ?? err?.status ?? err?.response?.status;
  if (code === 'RATE_LIMIT' || code === 429) {
    await backoffAndRetry();
  } else {
    throw err;
  }
}
```
kevin: Proposed mapping rows for PR: - v1 429 -> v2 'RATE_LIMIT' (retryable) - v1 502/503 -> v2 'TRANSIENT_SERVER_ERROR' (retryable w/ jitter) - v1 400 -> v2 'INVALID_REQUEST' (do not retry)
